<DocsLayout
  title="Attributions"
  description="Licenses and data-source attributions for lumen: Apache-2.0, CrUX CC BY 4.0, Tranco, Open PageRank, Wikimedia, and design notes."
  activeHref="/docs/attributions/"
  toc={[
    { id: 'license', label: 'License' },
    { id: 'crux', label: 'CrUX' },
    { id: 'tranco', label: 'Tranco' },
    { id: 'openpagerank', label: 'Open PageRank' },
    { id: 'wikimedia', label: 'Wikimedia' },
    { id: 'design', label: 'Design note' },
    { id: 'trademarks', label: 'Trademarks' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    lumen is honest about its sources because it has to be — and because
    attribution is the polite settlement for building on things people give
    away. This page is the complete list.
  </p>

  <h2 id="license">License</h2>
  <p>
    lumen is released under the{' '}
    <a href={locked.licenseUrl}>Apache License 2.0</a>. The canonical text
    lives in the repository root.
  </p>

  <h2 id="crux">Chrome UX Report (CrUX)</h2>
  <p>
    Field data — real-user Core Web Vitals — comes from the Chrome UX Report.
    Per Google’s terms: <em>“The CrUX datasets from Google are licensed under
    the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International license.”</em>{' '}
    Accordingly, any CrUX-derived value lumen shows is labeled with its
    source, and this notice applies wherever that data appears.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0 license text</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/crux/methodology">CrUX methodology</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="tranco">Tranco</h2>
  <p>
    Top-site ranking data comes from the{' '}
    <a href="https://tranco-list.eu/">Tranco list</a>, whose terms require
    attribution: Victor Le Pochat, Tom Van Goethem, Samaneh
    Tajalizadehkhoob, Maciej Korczyński, and Wouter Joosen, “Tranco: A
    Research-Oriented Top Sites Ranking Hardened Against Manipulation”,
    28th USENIX Security Symposium (2019). lumen caches the list locally and
    labels every derived rank with its source.
  </p>

  <h2 id="openpagerank">Open PageRank</h2>
  <p>
    Domain page-rank scores come from{' '}
    <a href="https://openpagerank.keywordseverywhere.com/docs">Open PageRank</a>{' '}
    (browser-extension crawl data, distributed via Keywords Everywhere).
    Factual reference; scores are labeled with the provider wherever shown.
  </p>

  <h2 id="wikimedia">Wikimedia</h2>
  <p>
    Pageview counts used as a demand proxy come from the{' '}
    <a href="https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Wikimedia_APIs/Guidelines">Wikimedia
    APIs</a>, whose guidelines require a meaningful User-Agent with contact
    information — lumen sends one, and honors 429s and Retry-After.
  </p>

  <h2 id="design">Design note</h2>
  <p>
    Visual design inspired by pi.dev; tokens reimplemented from scratch. The
    resemblance is a matter of palette and typography vocabulary — every
    asset, wordmark, figure and sentence on this site was authored for
    lumen.
  </p>

  <h2 id="trademarks">Trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    Product names and marks mentioned here — Google, Chrome, Lighthouse,
    PageSpeed Insights, CrUX, Tranco, Open PageRank, DuckDuckGo, Wikipedia,
    Claude, Cursor, VS Code, pi.dev — are property of their respective
    owners. They appear for factual reference only, and their appearance
    implies no endorsement of lumen.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
